### triage-agent — dry-run (AI Agent, experimental)
### Runs the published sys-agents component once on sample data: no instance, no journal, no session,
### and every tool answers a stub. Publish the agent first (wf sync).
###
### The runtime only allows callers whose role is listed in AiAgent:DryRun:Roles (orchestration host
### configuration; empty disables the endpoint and answers 403). Set @role to one of those roles.
### The same request from the CLI: wf agent dry-run triage-agent --data data.json --prompt "..." --role <role>
###
### "prompt" may use the state template placeholders over "data" (double braces around data.message, as
### in Workflows/triage-flow.json); they are left out here because HTTP clients read double braces as
### their own variables.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4201
@apiVersion = 1
@domain = core
@agent = triage-agent
@role = agent-tester

### Dry-run without candidates: the agent only produces its output
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/definitions/agents/{{agent}}/dry-run
Content-Type: application/json
role: {{role}}

{
  "prompt": "<message>Where is my card?</message>",
  "data": {
    "message": "Where is my card?"
  }
}

### Dry-run with candidates: the output gains a required decision (one of the candidate keys) and a reason
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/definitions/agents/{{agent}}/dry-run
Content-Type: application/json
role: {{role}}

{
  "prompt": "<message>Someone used my card without my permission.</message>",
  "data": {
    "message": "Someone used my card without my permission."
  },
  "candidates": [
    { "key": "is-question", "when": "The customer asks for information.", "whenSource": "description" },
    { "key": "is-fraud", "when": "The customer reports fraud.", "whenSource": "description" }
  ]
}

### Dry-run a specific agent version (latest when omitted)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/definitions/agents/{{agent}}/dry-run?version=1.0.0
Content-Type: application/json
role: {{role}}

{
  "prompt": "<message>What are your opening hours?</message>",
  "data": {
    "message": "What are your opening hours?"
  }
}
